            "notes": "Each LOG opcode charges gas proportional to topics and data size, naturally limiting total logs per block."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Identify the bloom filter construction code path that processes logs from transactions.\n2. Analyze the LOG0-LOG4 opcode gas costs and verify they are proportional to topics count and data size.\n3. Calculate the theoretical maximum number of add_to_bloom calls possible within the block gas limit (30M gas).\n4. Craft a transaction that maximizes log emissions while staying within gas limits and measure bloom filter processing time.\n5. Compare the bloom filter processing time ratio to gas consumed - verify no disproportionate amplification exists.\n6. Test with blocks containing maximum possible logs and verify bloom construction completes within acceptable time bounds.\n7. Verify that bloom filter construction cannot be exploited to cause client resource exhaustion.",
